# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 2, "The replacement", and Appendix B, `Replace`: `$n` takes all the digits that follow (`$1x` is group 1 then `x`), `${name}` a named group, `$$` a `$`; a group that took no part copies nothing; the escapes write `\n`, a tab, `/`, `\` and the code point named; every match the iteration rule finds is replaced (`a*` over "baaa" matches empty at 0 and 1-4, so "-b-"; the empty pattern matches at every character boundary).
